# Chapter Five — Tower Green.
# Question: where is Iris Marlow right now?
# Beats: the Mayor's shame, Nona's hidden key, and a bird who lands on you.

@node ch5_green_open
  Up close the Prismworks is not grand. It is a working building with forty
  years of small repairs on it, all of them done by somebody who meant it.
  The Mayor is standing on the green with his hat in his hands again, at the
  exact distance from the door that means he does not want to be nearer.

@node mayor_intro
  [if flag ch5.met_mayor == 0]
  MAYOR(shifty): Detective! Splendid. Splendid. Nothing to report, I expect.
  YOU:
    * (curious) A great deal to report. You have been avoiding this hill.  -> mayor_avoid
    * (kind) You do not have to stand out here if it upsets you.  -> mayor_upset
    * (dry) I have four days of your town's savings and a great deal to say.  -> mayor_avoid
  [else]
  goto mayor_after
  [end]

@node mayor_upset
  MAYOR(moved): ...That is the first kind thing anybody has said to me since
  Tuesday. I shall probably be unbearable about it later.
  trust mayor 1
  goto mayor_avoid

@node mayor_avoid
  set ch5.met_mayor = 1
  MAYOR(worried): I have not been avoiding it. I have been extremely busy
  with — with municipal —
  MAYOR(sad): I have been avoiding it.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Why?  -> mayor_why
    * (curious) Since the festival stopped, I think.  -> mayor_since
    * (dry) Municipal what, Mayor?  -> mayor_why

@node mayor_since
  MAYOR(sad): ...Yes. Since the festival stopped.
  goto mayor_why

@node mayor_why
  MAYOR: You will want the ledger. To see the ledger you must stamp the
  forms, and I am afraid that is not me being obstructive, that is genuinely
  the law and I have read it twice hoping it was not.
  start_puzzle stamp_order
  MAYOR(laughing): Six forms. Nobody has ever done that in one go. I am
  delighted and slightly frightened.
  MAYOR(sad): There. Line eleven. Festival of Lanterns, provision for.
  grant clue.budget_cut
  MAYOR: I cut it. Not postponed. Cut. Second year running, quietly, in a
  meeting with three people in it, and then I let the town believe it was the
  weather and then the apathy.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Why does that frighten you so much? It is a budget line.  -> mayor_shame_a
    * (curious) Why cut it at all?  -> mayor_shame_b
    * (dry) That is a very small crime to be this frightened of.  -> mayor_shame_a

@node mayor_shame_b
  MAYOR: Because the harbour wall needed doing and I had one pot of money and
  I made a choice a mayor makes.
  goto mayor_shame_a

@node mayor_shame_a
  MAYOR(sad): Because it was not the money. I could have found the money.
  MAYOR(sad): It was that only eleven people came the year before, and I did
  not want to stand on this hill and watch it be eleven again. So I cancelled
  it rather than watch it fail.
  grant clue.mayor_shame
  YOU:
    * (kind) That is not a crime. That is just being frightened.  -> mayor_forgive
    * (curious) And then the colour started going.  -> mayor_then
    * (dry) You cancelled a party out of stage fright.  -> mayor_forgive

@node mayor_then
  MAYOR(worried): And then the colour started going, and I told myself that
  had nothing to do with anything, every day, for two years.
  goto mayor_forgive

@node mayor_forgive
  MAYOR(moved): You are being very decent about this and I would rather you
  shouted.
  set ch5.mayor_done = 1
  trust mayor 1

@node mayor_after
  [if flag ch5.mayor_done == 1]
  [if not flag ch5.pip_done]
  [if all clue.fish_pail clue.tansy_saw clue.shiny_thefts]
  goto ch5_pip
  [end]
  [end]
  MAYOR: Nona Ember. The lodge, round the side. She lit that Prism for forty
  years and I stopped sending anybody to ask her. Start there. Please.
  [else]
  MAYOR: The forms, detective. I am sorry. I truly am.
  goto mayor_why
  [end]

@node wick_intro
  [if flag ch5.met_wick == 0]
  WICK: Mm. You have got up here at last.
  WICK: She has been talking about it. The tower, I mean. She creaks
  differently when she has got something in her.
  YOU:
    * (kind) What is she saying?  -> wick_saying
    * (curious) There is a second key, is there not?  -> wick_key
    * (dry) The tower is talking. Excellent. Everyone else has.  -> wick_saying
  [else]
  goto wick_after
  [end]

@node wick_saying
  WICK(sad): That her top stair is gone. I have known it a year. I put a
  bootlace across it and I told the council twice and it went in a folder.
  goto wick_key

@node wick_key
  set ch5.met_wick = 1
  WICK: There were always two keys. Tinter's and lamplighter's. Everyone in
  this town has forgotten the second one because the second one stopped being
  needed.
  grant clue.spare_key
  WICK: And the door has a word on it before the key does. The rings on the
  lintel. Old work, and it wants doing properly.
  start_puzzle mechanism_key
  WICK(moved): Aye. That is the word. She has said it to me a thousand times
  and I have never once said it back.
  WICK(worried): Now go and look at the stair with me, because I want a
  witness to what I am about to be right about.
  WICK: Rotten through, two-thirds up. The whole upper flight. If you went
  up that in the dark carrying something, you would not be coming down it.
  grant clue.stair_rotten
  set ch5.wick_done = 1
  trust wick 1

@node wick_after
  [if flag ch5.wick_done == 1]
  [if not flag ch5.pip_done]
  [if all clue.fish_pail clue.tansy_saw clue.shiny_thefts]
  goto ch5_pip
  [end]
  [end]
  WICK: Nona has the second key or she has not. Either way she knows where it
  went. Ask her gently.
  [else]
  WICK: Mm. The lintel first.
  goto wick_key
  [end]

@node ch5_pip
  [if flag ch5.pip_done == 1]
  Pip is on the low wall with his head tipped sideways, waiting to see what
  you do next. He has decided about you. It took a week and a pail of fish.
  [else]
  Something lands on the wall beside you, hard, the way a thing lands when it
  has been deciding for a long time and then stopped deciding.
  It is Pip. Up close he is smaller than the town's opinion of him, and he is
  holding something in his beak, and he is watching your hands.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Hold out your hand and wait.  -> pip_hand
    * (curious) Stay very still and look at what he is holding.  -> pip_look
    * (dry) Say nothing. He has heard quite enough talking.  -> pip_hand
  [end]

@node pip_look
  It is a brass letter-opener. Felix's. He is not hiding it. He is showing it
  to you, and then he is looking at the tower, and then back at you.
  goto pip_trust

@node pip_hand
  He hops onto your wrist. He is nine ounces of nerve and his feet are cold.
  He puts a brass letter-opener into your palm, which is not a gift; it is an
  argument he has been trying to make to this town for a week.
  goto pip_trust

@node pip_trust
  He goes up. Not away — up, to the roped-off landing, and back, and up
  again, exactly the way Tansy said, exactly the way you pull somebody's
  sleeve.
  grant clue.pip_trusts
  trust pip 3
  set ch5.pip_done = 1
  You have been in this town four days and the only witness has been trying
  to give evidence the entire time.

@node nona_intro
  [if flag ch5.met_nona == 0]
  NONA(worried): I know why you are here and I have already said it. It is
  lost.
  YOU:
    * (kind) I did not come about the key.  -> nona_notkey
    * (curious) Lost is a strange word for a woman who hangs her kit in order.  -> nona_order
    * (dry) Lost. In this house.  -> nona_order
  [else]
  goto nona_after
  [end]

@node nona_notkey
  NONA(moved): ...Then why did you come?
  YOU:
    * (kind) Because nobody has been up here in three years.  -> nona_three
    * (curious) Because you lit that Prism for forty years and nobody has asked you about it.  -> nona_three

@node nona_order
  NONA(shifty): Everything in this house is in order. That is not the same as
  everything in this house being findable.
  goto nona_three

@node nona_three
  set ch5.met_nona = 1
  NONA(sad): Forty years. My mother did it before me and hers before her, and
  then one year the council did not write, and I waited to be asked, and I am
  still waiting, and I am eighty-one.
  YOU:
    * (kind) You could have gone up anyway.  -> nona_anyway
    * (curious) So you hid the key.  -> nona_hid
    * (dry) You have been sulking magnificently.  -> nona_anyway

@node nona_anyway
  NONA(sad): I could. Yes. It was not a lock that stopped me, it was not
  being wanted, and those feel the same from inside.
  goto nona_hid

@node nona_hid
  NONA(worried): I put it somewhere. On purpose. I could not bear it hanging
  by the door being not needed.
  grant clue.nona_grief
  NONA: And now I cannot say where, because saying where means saying why,
  and I have not said why out loud in three years.
  NONA(happy): But I will show you the trick, if you like. The lamp trick.
  Everyone should know one useless beautiful thing.
  start_puzzle mirror_light
  NONA(moved): There. Light where light does not go. That is the whole job,
  really. Forty years of it.
  NONA(sad): It is under the third lamp on the green. I put it under the
  third lamp because that is where I used to stand, and I wanted it to be
  standing there too.
  grant clue.nona_key
  set ch5.nona_done = 1
  trust nona 1

@node nona_after
  [if flag ch5.nona_done == 1]
  [if not flag ch5.pip_done]
  [if all clue.fish_pail clue.tansy_saw clue.shiny_thefts]
  goto ch5_pip
  [end]
  [end]
  NONA(worried): Do not go up alone in the dark. And take the bootlace off
  the landing before you do, or you will trip on the warning.
  NONA: And there is a bird on that wall who has been waiting for somebody to
  hold their hand out. It will not be me. My hands shake.
  [else]
  NONA: The lamp trick first. Humour an old woman.
  goto nona_hid
  [end]
